%% 14-runbooks-deploy — deploying a change to a homelab service (project-dev 9b).
%% Source of truth: src/14-runbooks-deploy.mmd. Generated outputs are never hand-edited.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    %% atlas-participant A github-copilot
    participant A as Agent
    %% atlas-participant R git
    participant R as Service repo
    %% atlas-participant M mcp
    participant M as homelab-mcp
    %% atlas-participant S linux
    participant S as systemd
    %% atlas-participant Y debian
    participant Y as User

    Note over A,Y: There is no CI and no staging here.<br/>The deploy gate IS the test.
    A->>M: homelab_health (BEFORE — record it)
    A->>R: branch, edit, ruff check + pytest
    R-->>A: real output pasted, not summarised
    A->>Y: state rollback path first
    Note over Y: git revert + restart<br/>keep the previous venv or commit reachable
    Y->>A: explicit instruction to deploy
    Note over A,S: agents never restart a unit<br/>without that instruction in-session
    A->>S: systemctl restart <unit>
    S-->>A: systemctl status
    A->>M: service_logs(unit) — check for errors
    A->>M: one real tool call end to end
    A->>M: homelab_health (AFTER — compare)
    alt health moved or logs show errors
        A->>S: git revert + restart
        A->>Y: report failure with output
    else clean
        A->>Y: paste before/after evidence
        Y->>R: human merge gate
    end
